 are sent as attachments. For text files, output is truncated to 2000 lines or 50KB (whichever is hit first). Use offset/limit for large files. When you need the full file, continue with offset until complete.","exposure":"direct","name":"read","parameters":{"properties":{"limit":{"description":"Maximum number of lines to read","type":"number"},"offset":{"description":"Line number to start reading from (1-indexed)","type":"number"},"path":{"description":"Path to the file to read (relative or absolute)","type":"string"}},"required":["path"],"type":"object"},"promptGuidelines":["Use read to examine files instead of cat or sed."],"sourceInfo":{"origin":"top-level","path":"builtin:read","scope":"temporary","source":"builtin"}},{"description":"Execute a bash command in the current working directory. Returns stdout and stderr. Output is truncated to last 2000 lines or 50KB (whichever is hit first). If truncated, full output is saved to a temp file. Optionally provide a timeout in seconds.","exposure":"direct","name":"bash","parameters":{"properties":{"command":{"description":"Shell command to execute","type":"string"},"timeout":{"description":"Timeout in seconds (optional, no default timeout)","type":"number"}},"required":["command"],"type":"object"},"promptGuidelines":["You can inspect PI_* environment variables for current model and session details."],"sourceInfo":{"origin":"top-level","path":"builtin:bash","scope":"temporary","source":"builtin"}},{"description":"Execute a PowerShell command in the current working directory. Returns stdout and stderr. Output is truncated to last 2000 lines or 50KB (whichever is hit first). If truncated, full output is saved to a temp file. Optionally provide a timeout in seconds.","exposure":"direct","name":"powershell","parameters":{"properties":{"command":{"description":"Shell command to execute","type":"string"},"timeout":{"description":"Timeout in seconds (optional, no default timeout)","type":"number"}},"required":["command"],"type":"object"},"promptGuidelines":["You can inspect PI_* environment variables for current model and session details."],"sourceInfo":{"origin":"top-level","path":"builtin:powershell","scope":"temporary","source":"builtin"}},{"description":"Edit a single file using exact text replacement. Every edits[].oldText must match a unique, non-overlapping region of the original file. If two changes affect the same block or nearby lines, merge them into one edit instead of emitting overlapping edits. Do not include large unchanged regions just to connect distant changes.","exposure":"direct","name":"edit","parameters":{"properties":{"edits":{"description":"One or more targeted replacements. Each edit is matched against the original file, not incrementally. Do not include overlapping or nested edits. If two changes touch the same block or nearby lines, merge them into one edit instead.","items":{"properties":{"newText":{"description":"Replacement text for this targeted edit.","type":"string"},"oldText":{"description":"Exact text for one targeted replacement. It must be unique in the original file and must not overlap with any other edits[].oldText in the same call.","type":"string"}},"required":["oldText","newText"],"type":"object"},"type":"array"},"path":{"description":"Path to the file to edit (relative or absolute)","type":"string"}},"required":["path","edits"],"type":"object"},"promptGuidelines":["Use edit for targeted changes. Batch changes to one file in a single call.","Each edits[].oldText must exactly and uniquely match the original file. Keep matches short and non-overlapping; merge nearby changes without including large unchanged regions."],"sourceInfo":{"origin":"top-level","path":"builtin:edit","scope":"temporary","source":"builtin"}},{"description":"Write content to a file. Creates the file if it doesn't exist, overwrites if it does. Automatically creates parent directories.","exposure":"direct","name":"write","parameters":{"properties":{"content":{"description":"Content to write to the file","type":"string"},"path":{"description":"Path to the file to write (relative or absolute)","type":"string"}},"required":["path","content"],"type":"object"},"promptGuidelines":["Use write only for new files or complete rewrites."],"sourceInfo":{"origin":"top-level","path":"builtin:write","scope":"temporary","source":"builtin"}},{"description":"Search file contents for a pattern. Returns matching lines with file paths and line numbers. Respects .gitignore. Output is truncated to 100 matches or 50KB (whichever is hit first). Long lines are truncated to 500 chars.","exposure":"direct","name":"grep","parameters":{"properties":{"context":{"description":"Number of lines to show before and after each match (default: 0)","type":"number"},"glob":{"description":"Filter files by glob pattern relative to path, e.g. 'src/**/*.ts'. Without '/', e.g. '*.ts', it matches file names at any depth","type":"string"},"ignoreCase":{"description":"Case-insensitive search (default: false)","type":"boolean"},"limit":{"description":"Maximum number of matches to return (default: 100)","type":"number"},"literal":{"description":"Treat pattern as literal string instead of regex (default: false)","type":"boolean"},"path":{"description":"Directory or file to search (default: current directory)","type":"string"},"pattern":{"description":"Search pattern (regex or literal string)","type":"string"}},"required":["pattern"],"type":"object"},"sourceInfo":{"origin":"top-level","path":"builtin:grep","scope":"temporary","source":"builtin"}},{"description":"Search for files by glob pattern. Returns matching file paths relative to the search directory. Respects .gitignore. Output is truncated to 1000 results or 50KB (whichever is hit first).","exposure":"direct","name":"find","parameters":{"properties":{"limit":{"description":"Maximum number of results (default: 1000)","type":"number"},"path":{"description":"Directory to search in (default: current directory)","type":"string"},"pattern":{"description":"Glob pattern relative to the search directory, e.g. 'src/**/*.ts'. Without '/', e.g. '*.ts', it matches file names at any depth","type":"string"}},"required":["pattern"],"type":"object"},"sourceInfo":{"origin":"top-level","path":"builtin:find","scope":"temporary","source":"builtin"}},{"description":"List directory contents. Returns entries sorted alphabetically, with '/' suffix for directories. Includes dotfiles. Output is truncated to 500 entries or 50KB (whichever is hit first).","exposure":"direct","name":"ls","parameters":{"properties":{"limit":{"description":"Maximum number of entries to return (default: 500)","type":"number"},"path":{"description":"Directory to list (default: current directory)","type":"string"}},"type":"object"},"sourceInfo":{"origin":"top-level","path":"builtin:ls","scope":"temporary","source":"builtin"}},{"description":"Run JavaScript that calls other tools. The input is raw JavaScript (not JSON, no code fence), run as an async function body in a QuickJS sandbox: top-level `await` and `return` work. No Node, file system, network, or timers.\n- `await tools.<name>({ ...args })` resolves to a string, or an object if the tool's declaration says so, and rejects with an Error on failure. A tool whose declaration returns an object resolves on failure too when it returned that object; check its fields. Calls still running when the script ends are cancelled.\n- Optional first line: `// @options: {\"max_output_tokens\": 10000, \"timeout_ms\": 60000}`\n\nGlobals:\n- `text(value)`, `image(dataUrlOrImageBlock)`, `console.log(...)`, and top-level `return` add output; `exit()` ends the script. With several text items, each starts with a `==> text N/M <==` line, and `console` lines follow the other output in one `<console_output>` block. `image()` also saves the image to a temp file and the result names its path.\n- `store(key, value)` and `load(key)` keep JSON values across codemode calls.\n- `ALL_TOOLS`, `await searchTools(query, { limit?, namespace? })`, `await describeTool(name)`, `await describeNamespace(name)`: find unlisted tools, such as MCP tools.","exposure":"model-only","name":"codemode","parameters":{"properties":{"code":{"description":"Raw JavaScript source.","type":"string"}},"required":["code"],"type":"object"},"promptGuidelines":["Use codemode to batch independent tool calls (Promise.allSettled), chain them, or filter large output, instead of many separate calls."],"sourceInfo":{"origin":"top-level","path":"builtin:codemode","scope":"temporary","source":"builtin"}},{"description":"# Tool discovery\n\nSearches over deferred tool metadata with BM25 and exposes matching tools for the next model call.\n\nSome of the tools, such as tools of MCP servers, may not have been provided to you upfront, and you should use this tool (`tool_search`) to search for the required tools. For MCP tool discovery, always use `tool_search`.","exposure":"model-only","name":"tool_search","parameters":{"properties":{"limit":{"description":"Maximum number of tools to return. Defaults to 8.","type":"number"},"query":{"description":"Search query for deferred tools.","type":"string"}},"required":["query"],"type":"object"},"sourceInfo":{"origin":"top-level","path":"builtin:tool_search","scope":"temporary","source":"builtin"}}],"callable":["read","bash","edit","write"]},"version":1,"visibility":{"projection":{"files":[{"bytes":4716,"path":"benchmark/reported-model.mjs","sha256":"fae674ff8d8fb8e65953b936ce3c0097a8148f0266a64845325be46a8e793596"},{"bytes":7224,"path":"benchmark/runtime/episode-evidence.mjs","sha256":"6b713b14acdca7f5d8b425608bc96da87579f7ca7306b2b50f5e37ccb03c1a6b"},{"bytes":12581,"path":"benchmark/runtime/episode-notion.mjs","sha256":"11efc949e4b6e8232a281db2e5fb67f576373bd1433582a5b5a7672e6c101c8b"},{"bytes":8725,"path":"benchmark/runtime/episode-policy.mjs","sha256":"74086119f793ab5d001b013db7e1cc9b62466084a3d2b0ccb58020e9675833ae"},{"bytes":47604,"path":"benchmark/runtime/episode-runner.mjs","sha